  'r.doc': 'ArcHive. Rent out your machine', 'r.skip': 'Skip to the steps', 'r.lede': 'Bring an Intel TDX machine. The agent pairs it with your wallet, Arc verifies its enclave, and each paid use of a service it runs pays you in USDC. Your bond makes cheating cost more than it pays.',
  'r.verdict': '{a} operators hold a bond on Arc and {b} enclaves are running. Each enclave reserves its product’s minimum bond: {m} for product #1 on this testnet.', 'r.verdict1': '1 operator holds a bond on Arc and {b} enclaves are running. Each enclave reserves its product’s minimum bond: {m} for product #1 on this testnet.', 'r.verdict.wait': 'Reading the bonds on Arc testnet', 'r.verdict.src': 'Read live from OperatorBond and the ArcHive API.',
  'r.where': 'Where does your machine run?',
  'r.m.cloud.t': 'An Intel TDX VM at a cloud provider', 'r.m.cloud.d': 'Phala Cloud (dstack): real attestation today, in a certified datacenter where physical access is controlled. Google Cloud C3 and Azure DCesv5 once the kit reads the quote through the Linux TSM interface (in progress).',
  'r.m.bare.t': 'Your own Intel TDX server', 'r.m.bare.d': 'A 4th or 5th gen Xeon with TDX enabled, running dstack: real attestation. Outside a datacenter, physical access is not controlled: sensitive products may require a certified cloud, and the bond caps the risk.',
  'r.m.rent.t': 'No machine yet', 'r.m.rent.d': 'Rent an Intel TDX VM on Phala Cloud (from $0.06 an hour), then follow the cloud path.',
  'r.rentHint': 'On Phala Cloud, create a tdx.small VM, open an SSH session on it, then run the commands below.',
  'r.path': 'From bare machine to paid enclave',
  'r.s1.t': 'Post the bond', 'r.s1.d': 'A single signature (EIP-3009) locks a few USDC in OperatorBond. Nothing is spent: each registered enclave reserves its product’s minimum bond, and only the free bond can be withdrawn.',
  'r.s2.t': 'Install the agent', 'r.s2.d': 'On the machine, one command installs archive-node, the operator’s agent.',
  'r.s3.t': 'Check the machine', 'r.s3.d': 'The agent checks Intel TDX, Docker, the clock, the network, the Arc RPC and the ArcHive API.',
  'r.s4.t': 'Pair it with your wallet', 'r.s4.d': 'The machine shows a code like HIVE-7K2P-QX9M. You approve it with one signature in the console, with no transaction and no fee, then the machine shows your address and asks you to confirm. Your private key never leaves your wallet.',
  'r.s5.t': 'Start the enclave', 'r.s5.d': 'The agent runs the product’s image in a sealed enclave and gives it a public address. A machine without Intel TDX is refused: there is no demo mode.',
  'r.s6.t': 'Register it, Arc checks it', 'r.s6.d': 'Registration sends the machine’s attestation to EnclaveRegistry, signed by your wallet. Arc checks Intel’s signature (DCAP), replays the boot log and compares the image fingerprint with the one the author allowed.',
  'r.s7.t': 'Get paid in USDC', 'r.s7.d': 'Each paid use settles on Arc and sends your share in USDC, in the same block. A registration lasts about 24 hours, and the agent renews it with no gap.',
  'r.p1': 'Held by the contract', 'r.p1b': '{n} {ops} bonded, {a} in total, read live', 'w.operator': 'operator', 'w.operators': 'operators', 'r.p6': 'Latest enclave admitted on Arc,', 'r.p6demo': 'See the check step by step in the demo', 'r.p7': 'Latest paid call, {a} to operator {o},',
  'r.act': 'The bond, the pairing and the registration are signed with your wallet in the ArcHive console. This app only reads.', 'r.act.btn': 'Open the operator console',
  'r.ops': 'Operators on Arc', 'r.ops.lede': 'Read live from OperatorBond, for each operator that has registered an enclave.',
  'r.c.bond': 'Bond', 'r.c.free': 'Free bond', 'r.c.res': 'Reserved by enclaves', 'r.c.enc': 'Enclaves', 'r.c.encV': '{a} active of {b}', 'r.c.agent': 'ERC-8004 agent', 'r.c.none': 'none',
  'r.rules': 'The bond rules', 'r.rules.lede': 'The OperatorBond contract applies them itself.',
  'r.rule.cap': 'Capped exposure', 'r.rule.cap.d': 'On your enclaves’ signature alone, the network never releases more than half of your available bond over a rolling 24 hours, all enclaves included.',
  'r.rule.delay': '7-day withdrawal', 'r.rule.delay.d': 'You can take back your free bond after a delay: time for any fault to be proven.',
  'r.rule.slash': 'Slashed on proof', 'r.rule.slash.d': 'Two different signed answers to the same request: the whole bond is slashed and the operator is banned.',
  'r.rule.machine': 'What the machine cannot do', 'r.rule.machine.d': 'Its key (arcop_) is for reporting and diagnostics. It cannot withdraw the bond or spend: only your wallet signs.',
  'pp.doc': 'ArcHive. Publish your service', 'pp.skip': 'Skip to the author’s path', 'pp.lede': 'Your service becomes an ArcHive product: operators run it in their enclaves, users pay in USDC, and you earn the share you set, without owning a machine.',
  'pp.verdict': '{a} {prods} on Arc, {b} running now.', 'w.prodPub': 'product published', 'w.prodsPub': 'products published', 'pp.review': 'Publishing is open on Arc: the registry takes any author, with no review.',
